 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Cassava: peel, wash, soak (ferment) for some days, grate, press out the water, then fry or dry → garri; or ferment and cook in leaves → bobolo (miondo), water fufu, kumkum.\nMaize (corn): dry, remove the grains, mill → corn flour for corn fufu (couscous) and pap; soak and ferment → corn chaff, akamu; roast or boil fresh cobs; brew → local beer.\nMillet and sorghum: dry, thresh, winnow, grind → flour for fufu and porridge (bouillie); ferment → bil-bil (local beer).\nMilk: boil or pasteurise to kill germs; add a little yoghurt (lactic acid bacteria) → yoghurt; separate the cream → butter; curdle → cheese (wagashi).\nGood hygiene (clean hands, water and tools) is needed at every step.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "f": "maize"
  },
  "problem": "Name two products made from {f} and the main step for each.",
  "steps": [
   "Dry grains are milled into flour for corn fufu.",
   "Grains are soaked and fermented, then ground, to make pap (akamu)."
  ],
  "answer": "Corn fufu (milling) and pap (fermenting).",
  "checks": []
 },
